:\n- The key is rows 8–9, columns 7–8: `2 8 / 4 3`.\n- The red (2) shape fills the top-left quadrant around the key's centre point.\n- In the output the shape is mirrored into the other three quadrants:\n  - across the vertical axis between columns 7 and 8, painted 8 (the top-right key cell);\n  - across the horizontal axis between rows 8 and 9, painted 4 (the bottom-left key cell);\n  - across both axes, painted 3 (the bottom-right key cell).\n\nThe other pairs confirm the same rule:\n- **Pair 3, first key** `8 4 / 0 6`. The 8-shape is mirrored to the right in colour 4 and diagonally in colour 6. The key's empty bottom-left cell produces no copy.\n- **Pair 3, second key** `0 1 / 2 4`. The red shape sits in the bottom-left. It is mirrored up-right in colour 1 and right in colour 4.\n- **Pair 2** has three keys. One of them is `8 0 / 2 3`. The 3-shape in the bottom-right is mirrored diagonally (colour 8) and to the left (colour 2). Nothing goes up, because the top-right key cell is empty.\n\n**Finding the keys.** I scan for 2×2 windows that contain at least 3 distinct non-background colours. In every train pair and the test, only the key windows meet this condition. Windows inside a shape have only one colour plus background.\n\n**Finding the shape.** For each key cell, take the 8-connected component of its colour that contains it. The key cell whose component is largest is the shape's anchor. The shape includes that key cell, so mirroring it also lands exactly on the other key cells.\n\n**Reflection formulas.** The key occupies rows r0..r0+1 and columns c0..c0+1. Mirroring across the horizontal axis is y' = 2·r0+1−y. Mirroring across the vertical axis is x' = 2·c0+1−x. Which of the two flips a key cell needs depends on whether it differs from the anchor in row, in column, or in both.\n\n**Test input.** It has three keys:\n- `8 2 / 4 3` around the 8-shape in the top-left;\n- `3 2 / 1 8` with the 1-shape in the bottom-left;\n- `1 0 / 2 4` with the 2-shape in the bottom-left. The empty top-right cell gives no copy.\n\nEach shape gets up to three mirrored copies. I emit one stage per painted copy.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    out = g.copy()\n    H, W = g.shape\n    keys = []\n    for r in range(H - 1):\n        for c in range(W - 1):\n            win = g[r:r+2, c:c+2]\n            cols = set(int(v) for v in win.flatten() if v != bg)\n            if len(cols) >= 3:\n                keys.append((r, c))\n    for (r0, c0) in keys:\n        best = None\n        for dy in (0, 1):\n            for dx in (0, 1):\n                y, x = r0 + dy, c0 + dx\n                col = g[y, x]\n                if col == bg:\n                    continue\n                comp = None\n                for cc in components(g == col, diagonal=True):\n                    if (y, x) in cc:\n                        comp = cc\n                        break\n                if best is None or len(comp) > len(best[2]):\n                    best = ((dy, dx), col, comp)\n        (ay, ax), scol, shape = best\n        for dy in (0, 1):\n            for dx in (0, 1):\n                if (dy, dx) == (ay, ax):\n                    continue\n                d = g[r0 + dy, c0 + dx]\n                if d == bg:\n                    continue\n                fy, fx = dy != ay, dx != ax\n                for (y, x) in shape:\n                    ny = 2 * r0 + 1 - y if fy else y\n                    nx = 2 * c0 + 1 - x if fx else x\n                    if 0 <= ny < H and 0 <= nx < W:\n                        out[ny, nx] = d\n                emit(out, f\"Mirror the colour-{scol} shape across the key at ({r0},{c0}) \"\n                          f\"({'vertically ' if fy else ''}{'horizontally' if fx else ''}) \"\n                          f\"and paint it colour {d}.\")\n    emit(out, \"All shapes reflected into every coloured key quadrant.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"objects":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Finding the shape.** For each key cell, take the 8-connected component of its colour that contains it."}],"selection":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Windows inside a shape have only one colour plus background."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"The key cell whose component is largest is the shape's anchor."}],"rigid":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- In the output the shape is mirrored into the other three quadrants:"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"The 8-shape is mirrored to the right in colour 4 and diagonally in colour 6."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"It is mirrored up-right in colour 1 and right in colour 4."}],"topology":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Windows inside a shape have only one colour plus background."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"25c5b564370d5ea72e5e8196172b059f7985f91fa9d1599c94359eaa9158be5f","task_sha256":"6e9896c2356bab875896a7a9e5bf5ad0f171ec86caaad68422ca6b9184d15b20","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
